course: dictionary
lesson: 8431
title: Small packets, big meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sachet is a small sealed packet that holds a small amount of something. You may know sachets of ketchup from a takeaway, or sugar from a café. When you meet the word, look at the words around it to check.
explain: «Oral rehydration sachets mix salts and sugar in water so the gut absorbs it well.» The sentence tells you what is inside the sachets: salts and sugar, which are mixed into water. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A small packet of salts and sugar fits, so sachets must be small packets.
explain: The same word can also mean something else. A lavender sachet is a small cloth bag of nice-smelling dried flowers, put in a drawer. The context, such as drawer or smell, tells you which meaning is right.
fact: A sachet is a small sealed packet holding a small amount of something.
fact: Sachets can hold things like sugar, ketchup, shampoo or medicine.
fact: «Oral rehydration sachets» mix salts and sugar in water.
fact: A sachet can also be a small cloth bag of nice-smelling dried flowers or herbs, put in drawers.
fact: In maths, sachets can be counted: 12 sachets in each box, so 12 × 5 = 60 sachets in 5 boxes.
exercise: «Oral rehydration sachets mix salts and sugar in water.» What is inside the sachets? | Ketchup and mustard | Dried flowers only | Sand and stones | *Salts and sugar
exercise: Each box has 12 sachets. How many sachets are in 5 boxes? | 50 | 17 | 65 | *60
exercise: Lily says a lavender sachet is a plastic packet of shampoo. What is a lavender sachet? | A plastic bottle of soap | *A small cloth bag of dried flowers, put in a drawer | A packet of sugar at a café | A large glass jar of tea
test: Sachet means: | A bag of sand for the beach | A large bottle of drink | *A small sealed packet holding a small amount | A tall tree
test: Each box has 12 sachets. How many sachets are in 4 boxes? | 16 | 42 | 124 | *48
exam: A café puts 3 sachets of sugar on each of 8 tables. How many sachets are there in all? | *24 | 83 | 38 | 11
